    "memoText": "\n \n                         VETO MESSAGE - No. 287\n \nTO THE SENATE:\n \nI am returning herewith, without my approval, the following bill:\n \nSenate Bill Number 6552, entitled:\n \n    \"AN  ACT  to  amend the civil practice law and rules, in relation to\n      permitting a plaintiff to recover against a third party  defendant\n      in certain cases\"\n \n    NOT APPROVED\n \n  This bill amends the Civil Procedure Law and Rules to allow an injured\nplaintiff to directly recover from a separate third-party defendant on a\njudgment  for  contribution or indemnification when the defendant/third-\nparty plaintiff fails to satisfy the underlying judgment upon which  the\ncontribution  or  indemnification  is based. In a conservative estimate,\nthe New York Compensation Insurance Rating  Board  determined  that  the\nfiscal  impact  of  this legislation would result in an increase of $150\nmillion in annual losses, which translates  to  approximately  an  11.2%\nincrease in insurance premiums.\n \n  I  support  the  public  policy  of this bill which allows for injured\nplaintiffs to be made whole; however, the proposed legislation is not an\neffective, nor a practical means to  that  end.  Numerous  stakeholders,\nincluding  the  State  Insurance  Fund  and  Workers Compensation Board,\nraised concerns with this approach, with many stating that  this  change\nwill  significantly  increase insurance premiums. Based on the foregoing\nreasons, I am constrained to veto this bill.\n \n  The bill is disapproved.                    (signed) ANDREW M. CUOMO\n \n                               __________\n",
    "signedDate": null,
    "signer": "ANDREW M. CUOMO",
